---
title: IKEA Meatballs
servings: 4
prepTime: 2.5hr
cookTime: 45m
description: "For a simpler recipe, Rosina frozen Swedish Meatballs worked great with this gravy recipe."
source: IKEA
tags: Beef, Pork
---

= Meatballs =
Combine the @ground beef{1%lb} and @ground pork{1%lb} and mix with your fingers to break up any lumps.
Add @onion{1}(finely chopped), @garlic{1%clove}(minced), @breadcrumbs{3/4%cup}, and @egg{1} and mix.
Add @whole milk{5%Tbsp} and season well with @salt and @pepper.

Shape mixture into small, round balls.
Place on a clean plate, cover and store in the fridge for 2 hours (this will help them hold their shape whilst cooking).

Preheat oven to 350°F.

In a frying pan, heat oil on medium heat.
When hot, gently add meatballs and brown on all sides.
When browned, add to an ovenproof dish and cover.
Place in the hot oven and cook for ~{30%minutes}.

= Cream Sauce =
Melt @butter{3%tbsp} in a pan.
Whisk in @flour{1/4%cup} and stir for 2 minutes or until slightly browned or fragrant.

Whisk in @chicken stock{2/3%cup} and @beef stock{2/3%cup} and continue to stir.
Add @heavy cream{2/3%cup}, @soy sauce{2%tsp}, and @Dijon mustard{1%tsp}.
Bring it to a simmer and allow sauce to thicken.

= Serving =
Serve the meatballs and sauce with your favorite @?mashed potatoes{}(optional) or @?mini new boiled potatoes{}(optional).
Don't forget the @lingonberry jam{} on the side!
